# Nothing from the archive enters git

This repository is public on GitHub. The archive holds private chats, meetings and work details.

- Eval queries, grades, item keys, turn ids, chat titles, quotes, per-query results and snapshots live
  only in the gitignored `eval-local/` (default eval dir, see `scripts/eval-dir.ts`).
- Tests, fixtures, README and docs use made-up content ("Ana and Ben: Garden Plans", `cursor:1111`).
- Comments, commit messages and migration headers carry aggregate numbers only, never a query, title,
  person or project name from the archive.
- Never print or commit secrets found in chat text.
- Before every commit, check the diff (staged and untracked) for archive names, ids and quotes.

```text
❌ golden.json in scripts/ with real titles and quotes
❌ // broke the title leg for the "Garden budget sync with Ana" chat (a real title)
✅ eval-local/sets/golden.json (ignored); the gate reads it via evalDir()
✅ -- concept queries nDCG@5 0.49 -> 0.61
```

The release preflight refuses tracked files under `eval-local/`. If something leaks, purge history
(filter-repo), force-push, re-tag, and re-check releases: a later commit does not undo a leak.
